## Feature summary (web, SideFX reference)

- Source: https://www.sidefx.com/docs/houdini/nodes/cop/heighttonormal.html
- Summary (EN): Converts a mono height layer into an RGB layer of surface normals. Heightmaps are rarely to scale, so an explicit scale is often needed to get the expected steepness.
- Résumé (FR) : Convertit une hauteur mono en couche RGB de normales de surface, avec une mise à l'échelle explicite de la pente.

- Inputs meaning: ["height: a mono layer representing a heightmap"]

- Key parameters: [{"name": "Normal Type", "meaning": "Signed (-1 to 1) suits geometry attributes; Offset (0 to 1) suits normal maps"}, {"name": "Height Scale", "meaning": "globally scales height before normals are computed; higher gives steeper normals"}, {"name": "Read Pixels outside Image", "meaning": "lets boundary derivatives read past the image edge, useful for seamless wrap textures"}, {"name": "Kernel Size", "meaning": "pixel distance used for the derivative; can reduce stepping artifacts"}]

- Caveats: ["Read Pixels outside Image can act like extrapolation with a clamp border; leave it off to avoid that.", "The output is a single normals layer."]

